# Crew and relationship beats, trait reactions, and inactive-friendly events.
# House style: content/STYLE.md.

# The Starbase stash: opened on a fixed day so the Sharpie hand is known by arrival.
card l_stash
type event
cat human
due
once
days 11 11
roles A
when cond A ok
text Behind a stowage panel on {A}'s ship, three ration packs that never made the manifest. Someone at Starbase wrote "you'll thank me" on the bag in Sharpie, next to a little drawing of a Starship with its fingers crossed.
do open dil_stash

card dil_stash
type dilemma
once
cat human
days 11 11
weight 1
duration 3
roles A
when !fired dil_stash
lean warm share keep
text The three packs from behind the panel are the good rations, the ones the galley ran out of first. They aren't on any inventory.
option keep | Keep them quiet | {A} thanks the Sharpie silently. The packs go into a personal locker, for the bad week every mission eventually has.
  set stash_kept
  mark t_stash
  who stash_who A
  morale A 6
option share | Hand them in | {A} turns them in, bag and all. The galley has an unplanned surplus for the first time since launch, and the bag is folded into the inventory binder.
  who stash_who A
  res food 3
  morale A 2

card stash_found
type beat
cat human
due
once
days 24 39
roles A B
when flag stash_kept
when since t_stash >= 10
when is A stash_who
text It's been a long week. {A} opens the locker without a word, tags one pack for {B} for the next transfer window, and eats the other on video with {B}, reading the Sharpie on the bag aloud like the back of a cereal box.
do bond A B 6
do morale A 3
do set stash_exposed

card beat_watch
type beat
cat wonder
once
days 8 11
weight 10
roles A B
when bond A B >= -20
text {A} and {B} stand the night watch together over the fleet link, each in a dark cabin. Earth is a small bright disc now, less than half the width of the Moon from home, easy to cover with a thumbnail. They each make a coffee at the same minute, as if that counted as sharing one.
do bond A B 6

card beat_argue
type beat
cat life
once
days 9 39
weight 5
roles A B
when trait A warm <= 10
text {A} and {B} spend a whole shift arguing on the fleet channel about what plays during the next burn. {A} wants silence, so every noise means something. {B} wants anything with a chorus. They settle on one song, chosen by the ground team, sight unseen. It's worse than either.
do bond A B -4

# Trait-driven reaction: what happens depends on how brave A is.
card glint
type event
cat wonder
days 11 30
weight 8
once
roles A
when trait A curious >= -5
when cond A ok
lean brave closer window
text {A} spots a glint keeping pace off the starboard side, catching the sun every few seconds.
option closer | Get a closer look | {A} talks Mission Control into a camera slew: a chunk of ice shed from the fleet's own tanks, tumbling, going to Mars with everyone else.
  var glints 1
  trait A brave 3
option window | Track it from the window | {A} logs its bearing hourly. By the fourth hour it's plainly tumbling, each flash a face of ice from the fleet's own tanks. The log is neat enough to frame.
  trait A curious 2

card galley_pump
type event
cat repair
days 8 39
weight 6
once
roles A
when res spares >= 1
text The galley pump fails for the third time this voyage. {A} lays the parts out on a towel in order, rebuilds it, and ends up with one washer it never needed.
do res spares -1
do morale A -2
